  "tldr": "One response-adaptive experiment must serve a continuum of quantiles whose variance-optimal allocations generally disagree. The focal object remains \\(\\Phi(r)\\), the smallest worst-case LIL-normalized width of an anytime-valid prefix-population QTE band attainable at whole-curve Neyman regret at most \\(r\\). The rebuilt construction derives its loss from the actual Horvitz--Thompson CDF increment, defines the evolving target \\(\\tau_t\\), exhibits an explicit stitched-inversion band and a nonempty fixed-population class, proves a functional LIL converse, and leaves sharp frontier attainment as the first-class open question.",
  "project_justification": {
